# Rye build residue: `rye build` also emits <name>.zig beside each module it
# compiles, and the `*.rye.zig` line above catches only the bridge files. Twenty-six
# of these sat untracked in caravan/ after one witness sweep, one `git add -A` away
# from the tree. Authored code here is Rye; the few genuine Zig files are named back.
*.zig
!rye/lib/*.zig
!tools/fixtures/**/*.zig
.zig-cache/
zig-cache/

# --- macOS extended attributes and Finder artifacts (host moved from Linux) -
# The Linux-host .gitignore above only named .DS_Store; the Mac host adds a
# wider family of Finder/Spotlight/TimeMachine/AppleDouble droppings that can
# appear at any nesting depth, so these carry no leading slash on purpose.
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.TemporaryItems
.VolumeIcon.icns
.com.apple.timemachine.donotpresent
.AppleDB
.AppleDesktop
Network Trash Folder
Temporary Items
.apdisk
Icon

# --- tools/ : ship the template, withhold the personal fill-in --------------
# The committed key-card.conf.example is the template anyone copies; the real
# key-card.conf holds one person's details and stays local. tools/.build holds
# the qrencode binary we compile on demand from the vendored source.
#
# WITHHELD BY BASENAME, AT ANY DEPTH -- and the reason is a near-miss worth recording. These five
# names were anchored to the room root as `/tools/key-card.conf`. The `20260823.144100` tools fold
# moved every flat entry one directory deeper, the room root no longer held that file, the
# anchored pattern stopped matching, and the very next `git add -A tools/` staged one person's
# host configuration for commit. A pattern with no slash matches the basename wherever it sits, so
# a future fold, a hand that drops the file flat again, and a room not yet invented all stay
# covered. Every one of these five names is unique in this tree, checked rather than assumed, so
# the wider match costs nothing and privacy comes before completeness.
key-card.conf
enclosure.conf
secrets.env
launch-cursor.sh
launch-zed.sh
# Tracked launchers (not gitignored): tools/cu/cursor-jail.sh, tools/l/launch-cursor.rish,
# tools/ag/agent-jail.sh, tools/l/launch-claude.rish, tools/l/launch-cursor-agent.rish
/tools/.build/
/tools/bin/

# --- Editor state inside the project (ai-jail durable ground) ---------------
# ONE ROOM FOR LOOP STATE (20260827). The six dotted state directories below were six
# of the 97 doors facing a lap that opened the root. They are `loops/` now, each
# subdirectory named for what it holds, and `read-scope.md` seats the room as a closed
# stack. The elder names stay ignored: a clone adopts its elder directory on the next
# launch (agent-jail.sh, cursor_jail_macos.rish), and an un-adopted one must never be
# committed in the meantime. `.mind-state/` is NOT adopted -- the byte-pinned
# `tools/l/chatgpt-mind.sh` names it and its SHA-256 is the MIND adaptation receipt.
/loops/
/.cursor-state/
/.zed-state/
/.claude-state/                              # Claude Code CLI auth under agent-jail
/.cursor-agent-state/                        # Cursor Agent CLI auth under agent-jail

/squashfs-root/                              # extracted Cursor AppImage — binary, not source
/Cursor-*.AppImage                           # downloaded AppImages at repo root

# --- Local key material — never tracked -------------------------------------
# The allow-list above already excludes anything outside the project, but we
# say it explicitly: a sandbox GnuPG home and any loose key files live at the
# repo root and stay out of history. These are root-anchored so they never
# touch crypto test fixtures inside rye/lib/std.
/.gnupg-rye/
/.gnupg/
/.ssh/
/.gh/
gh-token.secret
/*.asc
/*.gpg
/*.sec
/*.key
/*.secret

